      "side": 1,
      "message": "You don\u0027t need to do it for this one, but another practice you\u0027ll see a few of us use for cherry-picks is to take the gerrit cherry-pick command line and add \"-x\" to the cherry-pick. Then the SHA of the original change will be added automatically to the bottom of the commit comment. It can be helpful occasionally. \n\nAdmittedly, it\u0027s less helpful when there\u0027s a Merged-In as well, as that\u0027s also a good indication of where the change \"came from\".",
